Tagging one of the authors, @_ghorbani, who did a lot of groundbreaking work on Hessian spectra!
Quoting @Tim_Dettmers
@Miles_Brundage By far the most underrated paper that I know is about the first accurate study of full spectrum Hessian evolution during training: It explains so many things like lottery tickets, batch norm, residuals. It also debunks common learning rate myths and more.

New Video 🥳 This paper uses lots of compute to learn a single, unified LSTM-based optimizer on over 6000(!) different tasks, then uses that optimizer to TRAIN ITSELF! We're in full meta-land 😱
